.TH WIDL 1 2026-10-20 "w64devkit" "w64devkit Manual"
.SH NAME
widl \- compile IDL into C headers, proxies, stubs, and type libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B widl
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.br
.B widl \-\-dlldata\-only
.RI [ options ]
.IR name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B widl
compiles an interface definition, written in Microsoft's interface
definition language (IDL), into the files that declare and implement
it: a header for C and C++, proxies and stubs in C that marshal calls to
COM objects and RPC servers in other processes, and type libraries.
It is Wine's IDL compiler, version 11.5, as distributed with Mingw-w64.
It reads the IDL dialect of Microsoft's MIDL, but its command line
differs.
.PP
.B widl
reads one IDL file,
.IR file ,
and cannot read standard input.
It runs the file through its own C preprocessor, then parses it.
An
.B import
statement reads another IDL file for its declarations, and the generated
header includes the header of that file, such as
.I unknwn.h
for
.IR unknwn.idl ,
instead of repeating them.
Each file is imported at most once.
Inside a
.B library
block,
.B importlib
reads the types of an existing type library, such as
.IR stdole2.tlb .
With
.BR \-\-acf ,
an attribute configuration file is read after
.IR file .
.PP
With no option that selects an output kind,
.B widl
writes every kind that the input calls for: the header and the interface
identifiers always, a type library when there is a
.B library
block, client and server stubs when there are RPC interfaces, a proxy, a
registration script, and
.I dlldata.c
when there are object interfaces that are neither
.B local
nor dispinterfaces, and metadata in Windows Runtime mode.
Only interfaces outside
.B library
blocks count.
.SS Output files
Each default file name is in the current directory, and is built from
.IR base ,
the part of
.I file
after its last forward slash, with a final
.B .idl
removed.
.TP
.IR base .h
The header, selected by
.B \-h
and named by
.BR \-H .
It declares the types, the interfaces as C++ classes and as C vtable
structures with call macros, and the GUIDs, and includes
.I rpc.h
and
.IR windows.h .
The proxy, stub, and local stub files include the header by this name.
Its include guard comes from the base name of the header file,
lowercased and with each character other than a letter or digit changed
to an underscore, as in
.BR __hello_h__ .
.TP
.IR base _i.c
The interface identifiers, selected by
.B \-u
and named by
.BR \-U :
definitions of the GUIDs of the COM interfaces, dispinterfaces, classes,
and libraries, such as
.BR IID_IHello .
.TP
.IR base _p.c
The proxy, selected by
.B \-p
and named by
.BR \-P :
proxies and stubs that marshal the object interfaces, for a proxy/stub
DLL.
Its symbols take their prefix from the base name of the proxy file
without
.BR _p.c ,
with each character other than a letter or digit changed to an
underscore, as in
.BR hello_ProxyFileInfo .
.TP
.I dlldata.c
The list of proxy files in a proxy/stub DLL, selected by
.B \-\-dlldata\-only
and named by
.BR \-\-dlldata .
It defines the DLL entry points
.B DllGetClassObject
and
.B DllCanUnloadNow
through macros in
.IR rpcproxy.h .
.B widl
also writes it while compiling an IDL file when no output kind is
selected.
It then adds the proxy to the list already in the file, if any, and
leaves the file alone if the proxy is listed.
When it adds to an existing file, it also writes
.BR "#define PROXY_DELEGATION" ,
which it otherwise writes only when an interface derives from an
imported or local interface other than
.BR IUnknown .
.TP
.IR base _c.c
The client stubs, selected by
.B \-c
and named by
.BR \-C ,
which send each call to an RPC interface to a server.
.TP
.IR base _s.c
The server stubs, selected by
.B \-s
and named by
.BR \-S ,
which receive calls and dispatch them to the server's functions.
.TP
.IR base .tlb
The type library, selected by
.B \-t
and named by
.BR \-T ,
in the MSFT format, or SLTG with
.BR \-\-oldtlb .
A file holds one library, unless its name ends in
.BR .res .
Then it is a binary resource file, with a
.B TYPELIB
resource for each library, numbered 1 or by the library's
.B id
attribute.
A name ending in
.B _t.res
also gets a
.B WINE_REGISTRY
resource with the registry entries of each library.
.TP
.IR base _r.rgs
The registration script, selected by
.BR \-r ,
in the text format of the ATL registrar: entries for the classes outside
libraries and their ProgIDs, and, when there is a class named
.BR PSFactoryBuffer ,
for the interfaces it marshals.
In Windows Runtime mode, entries for the activatable runtime classes
instead.
Only
.B \-o
names it, and a name ending in
.B .res
makes it a binary resource file with a
.B WINE_REGISTRY
resource.
.TP
.IR base .winmd
Windows Runtime metadata, selected by
.BR \-\-winmd .
Only
.B \-o
names it.
.SS Search paths
A quoted
.B #include
is first looked for in the directory of the including file, and an
.B import
in the directory of the importing file.
Then
.B widl
searches these directories, in order:
.IP 1. 4
Each
.B \-I
directory, in command line order.
.IP 2. 4
The kit's
.I include
directory, which holds the Mingw-w64 IDL files, such as
.IR unknwn.idl .
.B widl
finds it relative to its own executable, as
.IR bin/../include ,
so the kit works wherever it is unpacked.
.IP 3. 4
.I /w64devkit/include
on the current drive, from the kit's build prefix, or with
.BR \-\-sysroot ,
.IR dir/w64devkit/include .
.PP
.B \-\-nostdinc
omits the last two.
An
.B import
name that contains a
.B /
or
.B \e
is opened as given, relative to the current directory, without
searching.
.PP
A type library named by
.B importlib
is looked for in each
.B \-L
directory, first in a subdirectory named for the target, such as
.I x86_64\-windows
or
.IR i386\-windows ,
then in the directory itself.
Then it is looked for in the kit's
.I include
directory, which holds
.IR stdole2.tlb ,
and last in
.I /w64devkit/include/x86_64\-windows
on the current drive, named for the target.
.B \-\-nostdinc
omits the last two, and
.B \-\-sysroot
does not apply.
A type library is never looked for in the current directory or beside
.IR file ,
so one there needs
.B \-L
with its directory.
A name with a path is still joined to each directory, so an absolute
path is never found.
.SS Preprocessor
The preprocessor defines
.B __WIDL__
as the version, 0xb0500 for 11.5,
.B _WIN32
as 1, and
.BR __FILE__ ,
.BR __LINE__ ,
.BR __DATE__ ,
and
.BR __TIME__ .
.B \-D
cannot change
.B __WIDL__
or
.BR _WIN32 .
Neither
.B _WIN64
nor
.B __midl
is defined, whatever the target.
.SS Temporary files
Unless given
.B \-E
or
.BR \-N ,
.B widl
writes the preprocessed input, and each preprocessed import, into a
directory named
.B tmp
and 8 hex digits, which it creates in the current directory and removes
when it exits.
If access to the current directory is denied, it creates the directory
in
.BR TMPDIR ,
or else in
.I /tmp
on the current drive.
An error other than a syntax error, such as an import that cannot be
found, can leave the directory and its contents behind.
.SH OPTIONS
Options and
.I file
may come in any order.
A short option's argument may be attached, as in
.BR \-Iinclude ,
or be the next argument, and short options without arguments may be
grouped, as in
.BR \-hp .
A long option may begin with one dash or two, and its argument follows
.B =
or is the next argument.
A long option may be abbreviated to a unique prefix.
A word of two or more letters after one dash is tried as a long option
first, so
.B \-win32
means
.BR \-\-win32 ,
.B \-ro
means
.BR \-robust ,
and
.B \-pr
is rejected as ambiguous.
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.PP
The options that select an output kind are
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-\-dlldata\-only ,
.BR \-E ,
.BR \-h ,
.BR \-\-local\-stubs ,
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-s ,
.BR \-t ,
.BR \-u ,
and
.BR \-\-winmd .
.TP
.BI \-\-acf= acf
Read the attribute configuration file
.I acf
after
.IR file .
It is preprocessed like
.IR file ,
and opened as given, without searching.
.B widl
never looks for an ACF on its own.
.TP
\fB\-\-align=\fIn\fR, \fB\-\-packing=\fIn\fR
Marshal structures as if their members are aligned to at most
.I n
bytes, which must be 2, 4, or 8.
The default is 8.
This affects only the proxies and stubs, not the header or type
libraries, so the C code must be compiled with the same packing.
.TP
.B \-app_config
Ignored, for compatibility with MIDL.
.TP
.BI "\-b " target
Generate code for
.IR target :
a CPU followed by a dash and further fields, as in
.B i686\-w64\-mingw32
or
.BR x86_64\-windows ,
or
.B mingw32
alone for i386.
The CPU field begins with one of
.BR i386 ,
.BR i486 ,
.BR i586 ,
.BR i686 ,
.BR i786 ,
.BR x86_64 ,
.BR amd64 ,
.BR arm ,
.BR aarch64 ,
.BR arm64 ,
or
.BR arm64ec ,
and a CPU alone, such as
.BR i686 ,
is rejected.
The target sets the pointer size, the calling convention details
encoded in proxies and stubs, and the subdirectory of the
.B importlib
search.
.BR \-m32 ,
.BR \-m64 ,
.BR \-\-win32 ,
and
.B \-\-win64
override its pointer size.
Without
.BR \-b ,
a command name that begins with a CPU and a dash, such as
.BR i686\-w64\-mingw32\-widl ,
selects that CPU, and otherwise the target is the CPU of
.B widl
itself: x86_64 in the 64-bit kit and i686 in the 32-bit kit.
The long form,
.BR \-\-target ,
takes no argument, so it cannot be used.
.TP
.B \-c
Write the client stubs,
.IR base _c.c.
.TP
.BI "\-C " file
Name the client stub file.
.TP
.BI "\-d " n
Set debugging flags to the bit mask
.IR n .
Bit 0x01 prints progress messages about type libraries on standard
error, and bits 0x08, 0x10, and 0x20 trace the preprocessor on standard
output and standard error.
The other bits listed by
.B \-\-help
have little or no effect.
Any nonzero
.I n
also makes both outputs unbuffered.
.TP
\fB\-D \fIname\fR[\fB=\fIvalue\fR]
Define the preprocessor macro
.I name
as
.IR value ,
or as empty, not 1, when there is no
.IR value .
A later
.B \-D
for the same name replaces an earlier one.
.TP
.BI \-\-dlldata= file
Name the dlldata file instead of
.IR dlldata.c .
This does not select it.
.TP
.B \-\-dlldata\-only
Write only the dlldata file, listing each operand as a proxy file by
its base name without
.BR .idl ,
and read no IDL file.
The file is written from scratch.
.TP
.B \-E
Preprocess
.I file
to standard output and exit, without parsing it, so
.B import
statements pass through unexpanded.
Other output options write nothing, but the file of each output kind
selected along with
.BR \-E ,
and the
.B \-\-local\-stubs
file, are deleted.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage message on standard error and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Write the header,
.IR base .h.
.TP
.BI "\-H " file
Name the header file.
.TP
.BI "\-I " dir
Add
.I dir
to the include search path.
.TP
.BI "\-L " dir
Add
.I dir
to the
.B importlib
search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-local\-stubs= file
Write to
.I file
placeholders for the
.B _Proxy
and
.B _Stub
functions that each
.B call_as
attribute in an object interface requires.
Each returns
.BR E_NOTIMPL ,
or a zeroed value when the local method returns another type.
Only interfaces outside
.B library
blocks count.
.TP
.BR \-m32 ", " \-m64
Set a 32-bit or 64-bit pointer size, switching the target CPU to its
counterpart of that size, as from x86_64 to i386.
The argument may also be separate, as in
.BR "\-m 32" ,
and other values are ignored.
The pointer size appears in the proxies, stubs, type libraries, and
registry entries, and the proxies and stubs compile only for a target
of the same size.
Of
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-\-win32 ,
and
.BR \-\-win64 ,
the last one wins.
.TP
.B \-N
Do not preprocess
.IR file ,
the imported files, or the ACF.
The Mingw-w64 IDL files need preprocessing, so they cannot then be
imported.
.TP
.B \-\-nostdinc
Do not search the kit's
.I include
directory or
.I /w64devkit/include
for includes, imports, or type libraries.
.TP
.B \-\-ns_prefix
In Windows Runtime mode, put the C++ namespaces in the header inside
.BR "namespace ABI" ,
and add
.B ABI
to the C names, as in
.BR __x_ABI_CDemo_CIFoo .
.TP
.B \-\-oldnames
Name the RPC interface handles
\fIname\fB_ClientIfHandle\fR
and
\fIname\fB_ServerIfHandle\fR,
instead of
\fIname\fB_v\fIM\fB_\fIN\fB_c_ifspec\fR
and
\fIname\fB_v\fIM\fB_\fIN\fB_s_ifspec\fR,
where
.IR M . N
is the interface version.
The header adds the
.B \-\-prefix\-client
and
.B \-\-prefix\-server
prefixes to these names, but the stub files do not.
.TP
.B \-\-oldtlb
Write type libraries in the older SLTG format.
This fails for a 64-bit target, for a library that contains or depends
on a coclass, dispinterface, enum, union, or module, and for an
interface derived from one in a library named by
.BR importlib .
So any interface derived from
.B IDispatch
fails.
.TP
.BI "\-o " file
Name the output file.
When exactly one output kind is selected,
.I file
names it, unless that kind's own naming option was given.
With no option that selects an output kind, the kind is chosen by the
end of
.IR file :
.BR .h ,
.BR .tlb ,
.BR .winmd ,
.BR _p.c ,
.BR _c.c ,
.BR _s.c ,
.BR _i.c ,
.BR _r.res ,
.BR _t.res ,
.BR _l.res ,
or
.BR dlldata.c .
A
.B .winmd
ending also enables Windows Runtime mode, and a
.B dlldata.c
ending acts as
.BR \-\-dlldata\-only ,
so the operands are names, not IDL files.
Otherwise
.I file
is ignored, as it is for any other ending, such as
.BR _r.rgs .
The long form,
.BR \-\-output ,
takes no argument, so it cannot be used.
.TP
.BI "\-O " type
Select the stub style:
.B s
writes marshaling code for each method, and
.BR i ,
.BR ic ,
.BR if ,
and
.B icf
all select the default, interpreted stubs driven by format strings.
.TP
.B \-p
Write the proxy,
.IR base _p.c.
.TP
.BI "\-P " file
Name the proxy file.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix\-all= prefix
Same as
.B \-\-prefix\-client
and
.B \-\-prefix\-server
together.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix\-client= prefix
Prefix the names of the client stub functions, and of the client
interface handle, with
.IR prefix .
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix\-server= prefix
Prefix the names of the server functions that the server stubs call,
and of the server interface handle, with
.IR prefix .
.TP
.B \-r
Write the registration script,
.IR base _r.rgs.
.TP
.B \-robust
Ignored, for compatibility with MIDL.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot= dir
Search
.I dir/w64devkit/include
instead of
.IR /w64devkit/include .
It does not affect the kit's
.I include
directory or the
.B importlib
search.
.TP
.B \-s
Write the server stubs,
.IR base _s.c.
.TP
.BI "\-S " file
Name the server stub file.
.TP
.B \-t
Write the type library,
.IR base .tlb.
.TP
.BI "\-T " file
Name the type library file.
.TP
.B \-u
Write the interface identifiers,
.IR base _i.c.
.TP
.BI "\-U " file
Name the interface identifiers file.
There is no option to undefine a macro.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-W
Warn about preprocessor macro redefinitions,
.B #undef
of undefined macros, and ignored
.B #ident
lines.
The Mingw-w64 headers produce many such warnings.
.TP
.BR \-\-win32 ", " \-\-win64
Same as
.B \-m32
and
.BR \-m64 .
.TP
.B \-\-winmd
Write the Windows Runtime metadata,
.IR base .winmd,
and enable Windows Runtime mode.
.TP
.B \-\-winrt
Enable Windows Runtime mode, which accepts
.BR namespace ,
.BR runtimeclass ,
and the other Windows Runtime constructs.
A file can enable it with
.BR "#pragma winrt" ,
or
.B #pragma winrt ns_prefix
to set
.B \-\-ns_prefix
as well, and either pragma overrides
.BR \-\-ns_prefix .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
The directory for temporary files, used only when access to the current
directory is denied.
.TP
.B TZ
The time zone of
.B __DATE__
and
.BR __TIME__ ,
read by the C runtime.
.PP
No other variable, such as
.BR INCLUDE ,
affects the search paths.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid command line, an input file that cannot be opened, an error
in the input reported with its location, a type library, resource, or
metadata file that could not be written, an interrupt, or out of memory.
.TP
.B 2
Another error, reported as
.B error:
and a message, such as an invalid
.BR \-b ,
.BR \-O ,
or
.B \-\-packing
argument, a text output file that cannot be opened, a library named by
.B importlib
that cannot be found, or
.B \-\-oldtlb
for a 64-bit target.
.PP
An error in the input is reported on standard error as
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fIfile\fR:\fIline\fR:\fIcolumn\fR: error: \fImessage\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
followed, except for preprocessor errors, by the source line with the
location marked.
When
.B widl
fails after it starts reading
.IR file ,
it deletes the file of each output kind it was to write, and the
.B \-\-local\-stubs
file, whether or not it wrote them.
Without an option that selects an output kind, that is every default
name except
.IR dlldata.c ,
so a failed run also removes the results of an earlier one.
.SH EXAMPLES
A small IDL file that defines a COM interface:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ cat hello.idl
import "unknwn.idl";
\&
[
    object,
    uuid(5bb3e1a8\-6f2b\-4d5e\-9c1a\-2f7d3e8b4a10),
    pointer_default(unique)
]
interface IHello : IUnknown
{
    HRESULT Greet([in, string] const WCHAR *name);
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate its header,
.IR hello.h :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl \-h hello.idl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate its proxy,
.IR hello_p.c ,
and the interface identifiers that the proxy needs,
.IR hello_i.c :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl \-p \-u hello.idl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate everything the file calls for:
.IR hello.h ,
.IR hello_i.c ,
.IR hello_p.c ,
.IR hello_r.rgs ,
and
.IR dlldata.c :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl hello.idl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate a proxy for 32-bit x86:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl \-m32 \-p hello.idl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write the header into another directory:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl \-h \-o include/hello.h hello.idl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Compile a type library,
.IR mylib.tlb :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ widl \-t mylib.idl
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The kit also installs
.B widl
under its target-prefixed name, such as
.BR x86_64\-w64\-mingw32\-widl ,
and the 64-bit kit adds
.BR i686\-w64\-mingw32\-widl ,
which passes
.BR \-\-win32 .
Each targets the CPU in its name.
.PP
Default output names are split from
.I file
only at forward slashes.
With a backslash path, such as
.BR src\ehello.idl ,
the outputs go beside the input, as
.IR src\ehello.h ,
the include guard becomes
.BR __src_hello_h__ ,
and imports and quoted includes are looked for in the current directory
instead of in
.IR src .
A name without a lowercase
.B .idl
suffix is kept whole:
.I HELLO.IDL
gives
.IR HELLO.IDL.h .
.PP
Generated C files, headers, registration scripts, and
.B \-E
output end lines with CRLF.
.PP
Paths, including the location of the kit, must be representable in the
ANSI code page and fit in
.B MAX_PATH
characters.
If the kit's own path does not, the standard IDL files are not found.
.PP
Unlike MIDL,
.B widl
does not read an ACF unless given
.BR \-\-acf ,
does not define
.BR __midl ,
and uses
.B \-U
to name a file, not to undefine a macro.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cpp (1),
.BR gcc (1),
.BR uuidgen (1),
.BR windres (1)
